---
import SiteLayout from "@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Intro from "@/components/Intro.astro";
import Career from "@/components/Career.astro";
import { TAGLINE } from "@/data/site";
---

<SiteLayout title="About · Ryan Saxe" description={TAGLINE} section="about">
  <Intro heading linkName={false} />
  <div class="about">
    <Career />
    <section class="bio" aria-label="Introduction">
      <div class="bio-text">
        <p>
          I’m the Global Director of Data &amp; Analytics at AB&nbsp;InBev, where I lead science and engineering for our
          global analytics products. I’m responsible for the technology behind all of them.
        </p>
        <p>
          I studied mathematics and computer science at New York University, then earned a master’s while researching
          machine vision for gait recognition at NYU’s Courant Institute. At PepsiCo I worked on deep learning for
          ecommerce, researched graph neural networks and transparent neural architectures, and was granted a patent on
          contrastive loss and anomaly detection.
        </p>
        <p>
          I joined AB&nbsp;InBev in 2021 to manage a team building machine learning for marketing efficacy and automated
          spend allocation. From 2023 I was the technical lead for every commercial application of machine learning,
          across sales, marketing and finance.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside work I build tools for working with AI agents. pair lets you work with a coding agent in the browser,
          where it explains code and plans changes for you to approve. byor enforces the code rules a general linter
          leaves out, in the editor, in CI and inside an agent’s loop. The Nightly Build turns a GitHub repository into a
          personal newspaper that AI agents research and write.
        </p>
        <p>
          Much of my writing and several of my projects are about Magic: The Gathering. I have written about drafting
          for StarCityGames and Draftsim, and I co-hosted The 540, a Cube podcast. I also built a transformer that drafts
          and builds decks, helped build the models behind CubeCobra’s card recommendations, and created Crucible, a
          Magic format inspired by roguelikes and autobattlers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  /* The card switches to one column when the page is narrow. */
  .about {
    container: about / inline-size;
    padding: 0 var(--g);
  }
  /* The introduction is one reading column under the card, on the page's left edge. */
  .bio {
    margin-top: 56px;
  }
  .bio-text {
    max-width: 680px;
  }
  .bio-text p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 27px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .bio-text p:first-child {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .bio-text p + p {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
  @container about (max-width: 760px) {
    .bio {
      margin-top: 40px;
    }
    .bio-text p {
      font-size: 15.5px;
      line-height: 26px;
    }
    .bio-text p + p {
      margin-top: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
